# **DeerAge Privacy Policy**

**Last updated:** November 22, 2026
**App name:** DeerAge
**Developer:** Trey Harper

---

## **1. Introduction**

This policy explains what the DeerAge app ("the App") sends off your phone, what we keep, and why. DeerAge does not require an account, does not show ads, and does not track you across other apps or websites. We do not sell your data.

---

## **2. Photos you scan**

When you run Age My Deer, Quick Check, or Score My Rack, the photo is sent to our server and on to outside AI services for analysis: Google (Gemini) and Anthropic (Claude). Some backup paths may use OpenAI models through Vercel's AI Gateway. These services return the age and score estimate.

DeerAge does not store the photo from a normal scan. It is used to answer that request and then dropped. Results are kept on your phone in History, and you can delete them there.

When you keep a pre-shot record, our server stores a signed summary of the result (age class, call, cues, time) and a fingerprint (hash) of the photo so the record can be verified later. It does not store the photo or your location.

---

## **3. Information we collect**

Everything below is tied to a random app user id that the App creates for this install. It is not your name or Apple ID.

| Data | When and why |
| --- | --- |
| **App user id** | Created automatically. Used to count free scans, apply purchases, and link the optional items below to your install. |
| **Purchase history** | Purchases go through Apple. RevenueCat, our subscription service, receives your purchases and app user id so the App knows what you have unlocked. We never see your payment card. |
| **Email address** | Optional. Only if you sign up for rut-timing alerts and an end-of-season recap, or type an email on a wrong-call report or cancel note so we can reply. You can unsubscribe at any time. |
| **Report photos and notes** | Optional. If you report a wrong call, we keep that scan's photo, the result, the age you type, whether it was jawbone-aged, and your note so we can study the miss. A second look on a report stores the second result. |
| **Harvest checks** | Optional. If you confirm a harvested deer, we keep the scan id, the confirmed age, how it was aged, and your note. |
| **Cancel-survey notes and poll votes** | Optional. Your answer and any note you type. |
| **Push notification token** | Optional. Only if you turn notifications on, so we can send update notes or polls to this install. Turning notifications off removes it. |

**Location.** Optional, and only while the App is open. Your GPS point stays on your phone. It is used to suggest your hunt region and to add the stand to a pre-shot record saved on your phone. Only the region name (for example, an ecoregion) is sent with a scan so the age estimate fits your area. We do not keep it on the server.

**Lease manager name or phone.** Optional. Stays on your phone. DeerAge does not read your contacts and does not send the text; you press Send in Messages.

**"Help improve DeerAge" switch.** Photo sharing through this switch is turned off on our side today, so nothing is stored. If we turn it on, we will update this policy and the App Store privacy details first. It will only ever apply if you switch it on.

DeerAge does not use advertising SDKs or analytics SDKs and does not collect crash reports.

---

## **4. How long we keep it**

- **Report photos:** kept while the report is open. Once the report is closed, the photo is kept for 1 more year and then deleted. You can delete a report photo sooner from Messages in Settings.
- **Email:** kept until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete it.
- **Push token:** kept until you turn notifications off or it stops working.
- **Other items above:** kept until you ask us to delete them.

---

## **5. Who we share it with**

We share data only with services that run the App:

- Google, Anthropic, and (on some backup paths) OpenAI through Vercel's AI Gateway, for photo analysis
- Vercel and Upstash, for hosting and storage
- RevenueCat and Apple, for purchases
- Expo, to deliver push notifications you turned on

We may also share information when the law requires it. We do not sell, rent, or trade your data.

---

## **6. Your choices**

- Every optional item above can be skipped.
- You can turn off location, camera, photos, and notifications in iPhone Settings.
- To see or delete what we hold for your install, email **treyrea@gmail.com**.

---

## **7. Children**

DeerAge is not meant for children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their data. If we learn we have, we will delete it.

---

## **8. Changes**

When this policy changes, we update the date at the top. The current version is always at **https://deerage.app/privacy**.

